  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4602.49 Interim control period",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-03-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4602.49 “Interim control period” means a one-year control period that occurs in each of the first and second calendar years of each 3-year control period. The term includes the first interim control period, which begins on the same January 1 on which the 3-year period begins, and the second interim control period, which begins on the second January 1 of the 3-year period.\n\nSource. #9283, INTERIM, eff 10-1-08, EXPIRED: 3-30-09\n\nNew. #9444, eff 4-3-09; ss by #10468, eff 1-1-14 (from Env-A 4602.45); ss by #12967, eff 1-1-20 (from Env-A 4602.50)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4600.html"
